/* =====================================================================
   DAASI-3640 | Step 6b: the v1.14 daily load run by hand in UAT
   The proc cannot be CALLed by any of your roles (it replaces
   DAAS_TEMP.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_TMP, which takes ownership of that table),
   so this file runs the proc's four statements directly, as
   DAAS_UAT_DEVELOPER, against a TMP table that role owns. The SQL below
   is the deployed v1.14 text, lifted from
   DAASI-3640_03_HETCMS_COMP_DETAIL_FACT_LOAD_PROC_UAT.sql by a script
   with three changes only: the batch id written in as 36400001, the TMP
   table renamed to DAAS_TEMP_WORK.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_TMP_DAASI3640, and the
   doubled quotes of the proc body undone. What it does not exercise is
   the proc's JavaScript wrapper (query tag, transaction, batch-control
   bookkeeping, error handling), so one task-driven run is still wanted
   before PROD.

   Use: once as the smoke run (stream empty, nothing written), then
   after the bump (06 part D) as the slice run. Then 06 parts F1-F3,
   F5, F6 as written; timing from part 4 below instead of F4(a).

   Run it in one worksheet, top to bottom, with "Run all" or one
   statement at a time in order; the BEGIN ... COMMIT must stay in one
   session. On any error between BEGIN and COMMIT, run ROLLBACK and
   nothing has changed, the stream included.
   ===================================================================== */

-- 1. Session. The primary role owns what gets created and must hold
--    CREATE TABLE on DAAS_TEMP_WORK; secondary roles add the rest of
--    your grants (the fact and raw DML from DAAS_UAT_DEVELOPER, the
--    stream if it sits with STREAM_OWNERS_UAT, the warehouse through
--    the AUTH roles). If step 2 is refused, make DAAS_TEAM the primary
--    role instead, since it built the other DAAS_TEMP_WORK tables; with
--    secondary roles on, everything else still comes from
--    DAAS_UAT_DEVELOPER. The bump (06 part D) can run in this session.
USE ROLE DAAS_UAT_DEVELOPER;
USE SECONDARY ROLES ALL;
USE WAREHOUSE DAAS_UAT_IT_ADHOC_COMPUTE;        -- or DAAS_PROD_IT_COMPUTE; note the size
USE DATABASE DAAS_UAT;
ALTER SESSION SET QUERY_TAG = '36400001_HETCMS_COMP_DETAIL_FACT_LOAD_PROC';

